#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:1
msgid "ADR-0006: Context, graph and execution model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P5.1–P5.10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:9
msgid ""
"Phase 5 turns isolated elements into systems (REQ-CTX-1 to 10): a graph "
"of elements connected by typed ports, executed on demand with caching, a "
"clock driven by timed actions, two operating modes with a digital twin, a"
" structured journal, files and generated scripts. These choices shape "
"every later phase (web editor, MCP server, hardware drivers), so they are"
" recorded here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:14
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:16
msgid ""
"**Graph.** A `Graph` holds elements under unique identifiers (explicit, "
"from the name, or class name and counter) and connections between "
"`PortRef`s. Connections are type-checked, single inputs take one "
"connection, and cycles are refused at connection time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:19
msgid ""
"**Pull execution.** `run(outputs)` computes the required sub-graph in a "
"stable topological order. Outputs are cached **per element** (all outputs"
" of an element come from one transfer call). Elements notify listeners "
"when a field changes; the graph then drops the cache of the element and "
"of everything downstream. Connections and removals invalidate the same "
"way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:23
msgid ""
"**Containers.** An element belongs to at most one container, a `Context` "
"or an `ElementGroup`. Groups are elements with **instance-level ports** "
"(`instance_ports()`), feeding their exposed inputs to the internal graph "
"through `Graph.run(..., feeds=...)`; child changes propagate up as field "
"changes of the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:26
msgid ""
"**Clock and actions.** Time advances only through actions and waits, "
"never with the wall clock in simulation, which keeps simulations "
"reproducible. `@action(duration=...)` computes the duration before the "
"action runs; `ctx.parallel()` blocks advance by the longest duration. "
"Time-dependent elements receive `values.time` and are invalidated when "
"the clock moves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:30
msgid ""
"**Modes.** The context executes every action: in simulation the method "
"body updates the virtual state; in operation a `Command` goes to the "
"element's `Driver`, the clock advances by the measured duration, and the "
"twin either keeps the simulated state next to the measured one or the "
"measured state is written back. Overrides keep chosen elements simulated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:34
msgid ""
"**Journal.** Entries are dataclasses kept in `ctx.journal` and attached "
"to `logging` records (`record.lumos`); records of other LUMOS loggers are"
" captured during runs. The origin (`python`, `web`, `mcp`) is a context-"
"managed stack set by the service layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:37
msgid ""
"**Files.** Context documents follow §10 of the specifications; arrays "
"above 64 kB go to a `.npz` sidecar next to the file, referenced by name "
"only (no paths). A JSON Schema of the envelope is shipped with the "
"package and published with the documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:41
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:43
msgid ""
"Caching per port instead of per element: no gain, since a transfer "
"function computes all its outputs at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:45
msgid ""
"Push execution (recompute on every change): wasteful for interactive "
"editing, where parameters change many times before a result is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:47
msgid ""
"Wall-clock time in simulation: makes runs depend on the machine and "
"breaks reproducibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:48
msgid ""
"Storing large arrays as base64 only: JSON files of hundreds of megabytes "
"for pupil maps or phase screens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:50
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:52
msgid ""
"The web interface and the MCP server drive the same `Context` API and "
"only set the origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:53
msgid ""
"Hardware drivers (phase 12) implement `Driver._send` and return `Reply` "
"objects; nothing else changes in the context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:55
msgid ""
"Compiled pipelines bypass the graph and call pure transfer functions "
"directly (ADR-0002); the graph is an orchestration layer, not a compiled "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0006-context-and-execution.md:57
msgid ""
"Plan numbering: the ADR planned as ADR-0006 for extended-scene imaging "
"becomes ADR-0007, and the later ones shift accordingly."
msgstr ""
